<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n12984" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Dēmărātus</span></b> ,
		i, m., <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Δημάρατος</span>. <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b>
			<i>A Corinthian, the father of Tarquinius Priscus</i>,
				<i><span class="en">Cic.
				Rep. 2, 19</span></i>; <i><span class="en">id. Tusc. 5, 37 <i>fin.</i></span></i>; <i><span class="en">Liv. 1,
			34</span></i>.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			<i>A Spartan king, colleague of Cleomenes</i>, <i><span class="en">Just. 2,
				10, 13</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Sen. Ben. 6, 31,
			2</span></i>.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>III.</b>
			<i>Father of Pythagoras</i>, <i><span class="en">Just. 20,
			43</span></i>.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
